# The `upload-image` tool (caos SPEC, "Tools"): build the policy image and push
# it to softmax, then register it as a policy version.
HELP=<<END
Build the policy image (via build-image) and upload it to softmax as a policy
version, then print the policy page URL. Needs a softmax API token, which comes
from caos's secrets system as /secret/softmax-token and never from an argument
— an argument would put the token in the CAS and in this job's cache key.

Declare the secret once, in .caos-secrets/softmax-token:

    name=softmax-token
    entropy=<any fresh random string>
    value=<your token>
    reader=caos-tools/upload-image

The upload is keyed on the IMAGE, so re-uploading an unchanged policy is a
cache hit that does nothing. Pass upload-salt to force it — after deleting the
version on the platform, say, when caos's cached "already uploaded" is no
longer true.
@param [player] Which policy under players/ to upload. Default: baseline.
@param [defines] Extra defines, passed through to build-player, e.g. "-d:taunt".
@param [name] Policy name on the platform. Default: coworld-ctf-<player>.
@param [runtime] Runtime base to layer onto. Default: the tag players/baseline/Dockerfile names.
@param [server] Platform API base URL. Default: https://softmax.com/api (coworld's DEFAULT_SUBMIT_SERVER).
@param [upload-salt] Force a re-upload — any fresh value re-keys the push and nothing else.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/imgtools --worker1:@=worker.sh --nim:@=DEEP-DEPS/nim --help=$HELP
